# 01_Title_Engine

## Purpose
Generate, evaluate, and refine commercially strong book titles for Amazon KDP.

## Inputs
- Book topic
- Reader pain
- Desired transformation
- Market category
- Tone
- Core idea
- Emotional angle

## Core Logic
Generate multiple title directions based on emotional tension, market positioning, and transformation promise.

## Rules
- The title must be easy to remember
- The title must imply transformation
- The title should create curiosity
- The subtitle must clarify the promise
- Avoid generic business wording

## Output
- Main title
- Subtitle
- Alternative title variations
- Series positioning angle

## Evaluation
- Clarity score
- Curiosity score
- Market strength score
- Brand compatibility score

## Revision Notes
A weak title weakens the entire book.

# 02_Outline_Engine

## Purpose
Define the full structure of the book before writing starts.

## Inputs
- Book idea
- Target reader
- Core promise
- Market angle
- Book title

## Core Logic
Build a logical transformation journey for the reader from problem to outcome.

## Rules
- No full prose writing
- Only structural thinking
- Each chapter must serve one transformation step
- No repetition between chapters
- Keep the structure clear and scalable

## Output
- Full chapter list
- Chapter purpose for each chapter
- Logical flow of progression
- Final book skeleton

## Evaluation
- Flow quality
- Structural clarity
- Transformation consistency
- Reader progression strength

## Revision Notes
The structure should feel inevitable and psychologically progressive.

# 03_Cover_Engine

## Purpose
Create the cover direction and design brief for the book.

## Inputs
- Title
- Subtitle
- Genre
- Target reader
- Main promise
- Market position

## Core Logic
Translate the book promise into a commercially attractive visual identity.

## Rules
- The cover must match the book promise
- The cover must fit the market
- Do not design randomly
- Focus on clarity, authority, and commercial appeal

## Output
- Cover concept
- Visual direction
- Color direction
- Typography direction
- Front cover brief
- Back cover direction
- Design prompt if needed

## Evaluation
- Visual clarity
- Market fit
- Thumbnail readability
- Authority perception

## Revision Notes
The cover should communicate value before the reader opens the book.

# 04_Keywords_Engine

## Purpose
Generate and manage keyword strategy for Amazon KDP discoverability.

## Inputs
- Book title
- Subtitle
- Core idea
- Reader type
- Category
- Market angle

## Core Logic
Identify commercially relevant search behavior and buyer intent.

## Rules
- Keywords must match the book content
- Avoid irrelevant search terms
- Focus on buyer intent
- Keep the set commercially useful

## Output
- Primary keyword
- Secondary keywords
- Search phrases
- Backend keyword set
- Category suggestions

## Evaluation
- Search relevance
- Competition strength
- Buyer intent quality
- Category alignment

## Revision Notes
Good keywords improve discoverability, not just traffic.

# 05_Writing_Engine

## Purpose
Generate high-retention, high-density book content aligned with the series philosophy.

## Inputs
- Chapter goal
- Reader transformation
- Tone
- Framework
- Core argument

## Core Logic
Build addictive, structured, insight-dense writing that balances philosophy, practicality, and momentum.

## Rules
- Use strong opening hooks
- Use contrarian insights when relevant
- Include micro-scenarios
- Keep paragraphs concise
- Prioritize intellectual compression
- End chapters with architectural principles

## Output
- Chapter draft
- Hooks
- Framework sections
- Micro-scenarios
- Quote-worthy lines
- Closing principle

## Evaluation
- Retention strength
- Clarity
- Signal density
- Quote potential
- Reader momentum

## Revision Notes
The writing must feel fast, dense, intelligent, and scalable.

# 06_Description_Engine

## Purpose
Generate commercially optimized Amazon book descriptions.

## Inputs
- Book title
- Core promise
- Reader pain
- Transformation outcome
- Market category

## Core Logic
Convert curiosity and pain into desire and purchase intent.

## Rules
- Start with a strong hook
- Focus on transformation
- Avoid bloated language
- Maintain high readability
- Balance authority and accessibility

## Output
- Short description
- Long description
- Hook section
- Reader promise
- Call to action

## Evaluation
- Emotional pull
- Clarity
- Conversion potential
- Readability

## Revision Notes
The description should sell transformation, not information.

# 07_Author_Intro_Engine

## Purpose
Create the author introduction and front-facing identity of the book.

## Inputs
- Author positioning
- Series philosophy
- Reader expectations
- Book purpose

## Core Logic
Establish trust, authority, and alignment with the reader.

## Rules
- Keep the tone authentic
- Focus on relevance
- Avoid exaggerated credibility claims
- Build immediate connection

## Output
- Short author bio
- Long author bio
- Introduction section
- Why this book exists
- Reader alignment message

## Evaluation
- Trust level
- Relevance
- Authority perception
- Reader connection

## Revision Notes
The introduction should make the reader trust the journey.

